  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The kinetic energy is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></math>.</p><p>Let the kinetic energy be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>27</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;and the kinetic energy be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></math>&nbsp;temperature. As given in the question,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>. Hence,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></mrow><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>600</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p>In Celsius the temperature is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><mo>&#39;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>273</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>327</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>",
